--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS SOFTWARE IS NOT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A phone camera is a three-channel device. It is not a spectrophotometer: it
cannot observe a spectrum, it cannot see metamerism, and it estimates
translucency rather than measuring it. Every result this software produces
carries a confidence score, and a result read without its confidence score is
being read wrongly.

This software is not a medical device and is not a diagnostic instrument. It
does not replace a shade guide, a spectrophotometer, or a clinician's judgement.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE SHIPPED SHADE VALUES ARE A SCAFFOLD, NOT MEASUREMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The shade libraries in this repository (VITA classical, VITA 3D-MASTER and the
composite and zirconia tables) are a documented structural scaffold: the tab
names, their ordering and their adjacency are real, and the numeric L*a*b*
values attached to them are PLACEHOLDERS that have not been measured on a
spectrophotometer. They are generated, marked as unverified in the source, and
exist so the algorithms have something of the right shape to run against.

Do not treat them as reference data. Do not publish results computed from them
as colorimetric findings. Anyone shipping this software clinically must replace
them with values measured on their own instrument and say so.

